      },
      {
        "name": "LRO Pattern (SyncPoller/PollerFlux)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "No long-running operations are applicable for blob upload/download/delete. No Thread.sleep() polling loops used. Blob copy (which uses PollerFlux) is not part of this scenario."
      },
      {
        "name": "Async Uses Project Reactor (Mono/Flux)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Async service uses Mono and Flux from Project Reactor. No CompletableFuture or RxJava. The .block() calls are only in Main.java demo code, not inside the async service implementation."
      },
      {
        "name": "Service-Specific Exception Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No BlobStorageException or HttpResponseException handling anywhere. Main.java catches only generic Exception. No status code inspection on service errors."
      },
      {
        "name": "Code Compiles (mvn compile)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "BlobStorageAsyncService.downloadBlob() declares return type Mono\u003cVoid\u003e but blobClient.downloadToFile() returns Mono\u003cBlobProperties\u003e. This is a type mismatch compilation error. Maven was not available to verify directly, but the API mismatch is confirmed via official Azure SDK documentation."
      },
      {
        "name": "Try-With-Resources for Clients",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "BlobServiceClient and BlobServiceAsyncClient do not implement AutoCloseable in the Azure SDK, so try-with-resources is not applicable. InputStream and OutputStream in sync service methods are properly wrapped in try-with-resources."
      },
      {
        "name": "Configures custom retry policy (exponential backoff, max retries, delay)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "BlobStorageConfig uses ExponentialBackoffOptions with setMaxRetries, setBaseDelay, and setMaxDelay, wrapped in RetryOptions. Fully configurable via builder."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sets per-request or per-operation timeout",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "requestTimeout is configurable via the builder and passed to sync uploadWithResponse and downloadStreamWithResponse calls via the timeout parameter."
      },
      {
        "name": "Enables HTTP logging (HttpLogOptions)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "HttpLogOptions is configured with a settable HttpLogDetailLevel and setPrettyPrintBody(true). Applied to the client builder."
      },
      {
        "name": "Implements blob lease acquisition before overwrite",
