        "reason": "Uses BlobParallelUploadOptions (correct wrapper) but never explicitly configures ParallelTransferOptions for block size or concurrency. The async version manually chunks into 4MB byte arrays with blocking I/O inside Flux.create, which is manual chunking on the reactor thread — a serious anti-pattern."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sets blob index tags on upload",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "BlobParallelUploadOptions.setTags(tags) is called during upload with a Map\u003cString, String\u003e of index tags. Both sync and async services support tags."
      },
      {
        "name": "Properly composes reactive chains in the demo",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "The async demo in Main.java calls .block() sequentially on every operation. No reactive chain composition (then/flatMap/zip). This is functionally identical to the sync demo and doesn't demonstrate reactive patterns."
      },
      {
        "name": "Code Builds",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Compilation error: BlobStorageAsyncService.downloadBlob() returns Mono\u003cVoid\u003e but downloadToFile() returns Mono\u003cBlobProperties\u003e. Type mismatch prevents compilation."
      },
